      <Placemark><name>Aiyari old aidpost</name><styleUrl>#closed</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>aid post</b>, status: closed<br/>1 building(s) recorded<br/>Recorded in the field: "Three Community Health Workers (CHWs) served at this aid post before it was closed. According to one source from Aiyari, the last CHW served here around 1979, and the aid post was closed around that year due to distance and the tough environment."]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.2198087,-9.3514312,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Old aidpost</name><styleUrl>#closed</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>aid post</b>, status: closed<br/>1 building(s) recorded<br/>Recorded in the field: "According to two sources from Aiyari and Suari, this site is where the old aid post was built during colonial times and was run by white people. The dates when it was established and when it closed are unknown to both sources."]]></description><Point><coordinates>148.1797902,-9.3601343,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
    </Folder>
